  "id": "salvagerites",
  "neon": "#ffb43a",
  "note": "SALVAGE RITES — the scrapyard on Ironside Street, and the street's one real vertical.\n\nIt is bound by name and replaces nothing. `type:junkyard` draws four yards (Slag & Wares, Thumb On\nThe Scale and The Houndyard as well as this one), so a name bind changes this tile and leaves the\nother three alone.\n\nThe crane is adornment. A lattice derrick is open steel, and as mass it would enter CFIT\ncollision, the ground probe and the occluder hulls as a solid block. `latticeTower` draws it as\nstrokes. The bales are mass, because crushed cars stacked two high are a wall you can't drive\nthrough.\n\nThe frontage is the gate, because that is what the tile's prose describes: chain-link on a rolling\ntrack with wire along the top, rolled back so the yard is open, and a hand-painted board wired to\nit. The board carries the slogan and the office board carries the name, so the name appears once.\nBehind the mesh the bales stand in uneven rows of different heights, and the shipping containers\nsupply the three saturated colours nothing else on Ironside has; every other mass on the tile is\nwithin a few points of the same brown.\n\nA container is long and a box is square unless you say otherwise: `box` takes `fd`, the\nhalf-depth, and defaults it to `hw`. Every container and bale row here carries an explicit `fd`.\n\nThe torch on the crane is `s: 7`, under the size of what it sits on, because\n`AUTHORED_ADORN.glowPool` has no night term and a bigger one is a white blob at noon. The yard is\nlit by one sodium floodlight on a pole at the gate, which is amber because this is industry.",
  "pal": "ty_junk_shack",
